secubox-annuaire (0.10.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * fix: make /etc/secubox/secrets traversable by the service user. The unit
    runs as `secubox` and its node.key is secubox-owned, but the shared parent
    ended up 0700 root:root, so secubox-metrics-publish failed permanently with
    a misleading "no box key" — the key was there, the path was not.
    `chmod o+x` grants traversal only, never listing: sub-directories keep
    their 0700 and the secrets their 0600. Same geste as secubox-assist.
    Six packages write the mode of that shared directory and the last one
    installed wins; posting the rule once (in secubox-core) is the real fix and
    is tracked separately. (ref #952)

